            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0147" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-02T16:00:00-04:00">July 2, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1521. Your 1926, 2d. From Long. Glad to hear about the fine number of
                    bookings.</p>
                <p>Concerning refugee children it is now considered that in view of your
                    conversation with Shakespeare and in view of the limitations of our statutes you
                    might gracefully withdraw. There is no technical difficulty about alien mothers
                    coming with the children and that could be arranged, but in view of the
                    statement of Shakespeare and in view of the possible political inquiries which
                    might develop here it seems best now that these children be not placed on this
                    particular boat and that only American citizens be accommodated. However for
                    your general information and use as regards British boats the above situation
                    about alien mothers may be helpful. [Long.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
